WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
- You brought a clip of
your wife, actually, right?

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.127
- I did, so they asked
me, your staff said,

00:00:05.127 --> 00:00:07.587
"What's it like, marriage for 40 years?

00:00:07.587 --> 00:00:08.960
"How do you make it interesting?"

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.870
I don't know if I make it
interesting as I do annoying

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.320
and my wife, I'll show you.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.910
I brought this clip because
she got really mad at me.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.280
She did, it was her birthday

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.600
and I wanted to surprise my wife.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.030
My wife loves animals, any
kind of animal, she does.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.840
And we work for a preserve

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.053
and so I rented an elephant.

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:32.730
I rented an elephant and I
had it brought to the house

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.310
because I love her--
- You went big.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.810
- I did go big, but I'm not a good planner

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.030
and I have severe attention.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.490
I didn't invite anybody.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.370
I didn't cater.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.740
I didn't bring even a staff.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.680
- So, just like, an elephant showed up?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.460
- Well, let me show you the video

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.820
and then I'm gonna talk about the trouble.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.080
So, this is my wife's birthday.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.170
Watch what I did for my wife's birthday.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.433
Watch this.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:57.450
- [Howie Voiceover] This is
my wife's birthday party.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.320
That's my wife.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.153
Hi wife.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.513
(audience applauds)

00:01:01.513 --> 00:01:02.346
There's the elephant.

00:01:03.874 --> 00:01:05.583
And there's my wife.

00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:06.700
(laughs)

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.740
Okay, wait, wait.
(audience applauds)

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.190
- That's the saddest party ever.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.023
- There was an elephant there.

00:01:13.023 --> 00:01:14.580
- You didn't even have one balloon.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.250
- No, I had nothing and I'm so
stupid, I don't think of this

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.210
and also, because we care about animals,

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:22.001
you can't just bring
an animal for an hour.

00:01:22.001 --> 00:01:25.590
He had to be out of the transport thing

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.260
for at least 12 hours.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.100
So, the animal was in our
backyard for 12 hours.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.550
So, wait, wait.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:32.780
I don't have that kind of attention

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.740
and my wife was bored after a half hour

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:35.573
so we went in the house

00:01:35.573 --> 00:01:37.750
but elephants, they like palm trees.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.800
So, the elephant took
out all our palm trees.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.610
The elephant took them
out and laid them down.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.290
And then, the elephant--
- What?

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.236
- How much clearer can I make it?

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:48.410
(audience laughs)

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:52.070
And then, the elephant
needed to be comfortable,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.088
so they said I should hose him,

00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:56.060
so I hosed the elephant,
which made it muddy

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.170
and the the elephant, they're heavy,

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.900
the elephant sunk into my
lawn and broke the sprinkles,

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.260
all the sprinkler system--

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.220
- Happy birthday!

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.470
- Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.570
And then, I ordered food, not
for us, but for the elephant.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.352
The elephant ate and then the elephant,

00:02:10.352 --> 00:02:11.185
is very regular.

00:02:11.185 --> 00:02:12.330
The elephant is very regular.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.730
- Oh, my gosh.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.810
- That's what the guy

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.530
who came to our backyard the next day said

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.050
because there are piles of elephant--

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.150
- Dung.
- Poo.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.880
So, the next day, the
gardener, we have a gardener.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.999
Gardener came, comes around the corner,

00:02:26.999 --> 00:02:30.050
the yard is these holes
that are four feet deep,

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.310
the sprinklers are broken,

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.760
five palm trees are
laying all over the place

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.600
and there's a pile of...

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.360
You can put a bleep on (beep), right?

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.828
There's a pile--

00:02:38.828 --> 00:02:41.890
(audience laughs)

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.120
- Yes.
- Yes.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.570
There's a giant, there is
no, and the guy walks in

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:51.230
and he goes, "Mr. Mandel, what is this?"

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.965
and I go, "It was my wife's birthday."

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.080
(audience laughs)

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.592
- [Kelly] Nailed it!

00:02:56.592 --> 00:02:57.480
(laughs)

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.470
- I never explained,
there was $45,000 damage.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.710
The sprinklers, the trees,
- Oh, my gosh.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:07.215
- And elephant poo removal is
not a service that is nearby.

00:03:07.215 --> 00:03:08.048
(audience laughs)

00:03:08.048 --> 00:03:09.810
- So your gift to your
wife for her birthday

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.780
was just severely
pissing her off. (laughs)

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.360
- You know what, I'm consistent.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.260
I'm fairly consistent. (Kelly laughs)

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.780
It's not any different on her birthday

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.070
than it is each and every day.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:19.940
- [Kelly] It's important to be consistent.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.190
- You know what she loves about me

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.125
is that I'm here and she's not.

00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:24.290
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.920
She loves me being away.
- So she gets alone time?

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.570
- She gets alone time without me.

